deps.Transfers.SuspectedTransfers(). No call into ResolveTransfer, Snapshots,
Confirm, or Store. Confirmed deps.load() -> dataloader.LoadData ->
LoadDataContext does file reads (CSV glob, accounts.Load) and only
in-memory-state writes (dl.setUnassignedCount/setStableIndex/setTransferState,
mutex-protected caches) -- no disk writes found in the portion read. Parity
check: get_transfers.go (internal/services/mcpsvc/ledger/transfers.go) also
calls deps.load() unconditionally as its own read path, so triggering load()
is consistent with the package's existing "read-only" tools, not a new
exception carved out for this one. C's fake-recording assertion
(fake.resolveCalled) is exercised in the round-trip test and was proven live
by mutation 5 above.

